-- Raw dockerd replies, recorded over the daemon socket with an HTTP/1.0 and an HTTP/1.1 (Connection: close) request,
-- one set per daemon. Docker Engine (29.4.1, 29.4.3, 29.9.3, each in docker:<version>-dind) sets Content-Length on
-- both forms and ends the list bodies with a newline. Docker Desktop's own socket re-frames the same calls: no
-- Content-Length on HTTP/1.0 (read to EOF), chunked on HTTP/1.1, no trailing newline on lists. `ping.*` is GET /_ping,
-- whose Api-Version header is where the proxy reads the daemon's API version.
-- policy.lua must read all of them. Kept as escaped strings, not files, so line-ending normalisers cannot touch the
-- CRLFs. `id` is the container the list-one replies describe (labelled postern.managed=true, postern.instance=l11r).
